.TH "CSSMATHSUM" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSMathSum \- CSSMathSum
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathSum\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents the sum of two or more \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]
values \(em in cases where the result can\(cqt be represented as a
single value.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathSum()\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathSum.values\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericArray\f[R] object which contains one or more
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] objects.
.SH STATIC METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] is produced whenever an addition or subtraction
can\(cqt be resolved to a single value \(em for example, when the
operands use different units, such as a length and a percentage.
.PP
Calling \f[CR]add()\f[R] or \f[CR]sub()\f[R] on operands that can\(cqt
be combined returns a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R]; if every operand shares the
same unit, they resolve immediately to a single \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R]
instead.
\f[CR]toSum()\f[R], by contrast, always returns a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R],
even when its terms could be combined into a single value.
.PP
\f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly.get()\f[R] returns a
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] the same way \(em for a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] value
that resolves to an addition or subtraction it can\(cqt combine into one
value.
.PP
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] represents the sum expression itself, not a
resolved value.
To get the resolved value, use \f[CR]getComputedStyle()\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code creates a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] instance from three
values, then reads back its \f[CR]operator\f[R] and \f[CR]values\f[R]
properties.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sum = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathSum(CSS.px(10), CSS.em(5), CSS.percent(50));

console.log(sum.constructor.name); \f[I]// \(dqCSSMathSum\(dq\f[R]
console.log(sum.operator); \f[I]// \(aqsum\(aq\f[R]

console.log(sum.values); \f[I]// CSSNumericArray {0: CSSUnitValue, 1: CSSUnitValue, 2: CSSUnitValue, length: 3}\f[R]
console.log(sum.values[0]); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 10, unit: \(dqpx\(dq}\f[R]
.EE
.SS \f[CR]calc()\f[R] representations
This example shows how a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] addition is represented by a
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] or a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R], depending on whether
its terms share a unit.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqdemoBox\(dq>Text</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
\f[CR]width\f[R] is set using a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] sum whose terms are
both \f[CR]px\f[R] lengths, so the browser can resolve it to a single
fixed value immediately.
\f[CR]font\-size\f[R] is set using a \f[CR]calc()\f[R] sum that mixes
\f[CR]rem\f[R] and \f[CR]vw\f[R], so the browser can\(cqt combine the
terms until layout (this will be represented by a
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R]).
.IP
.EX
demoBox {
  \f[B]width\f[R]: calc(10px + 5px);
  \f[B]font\-size\f[R]: calc(1rem + 5vw);
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
First we find the demo box\(cqs style rule and read its \f[CR]width\f[R]
and \f[CR]font\-size\f[R] values using \f[CR]styleMap\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] demoBox = document.querySelector(\(dq#demoBox\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] rules = document.getElementById(\(dqcss\-output\(dq).sheet.cssRules;
\f[B]const\f[R] rule = [...rules].find((r) \f[B]=>\f[R] r.selectorText === \(dq#demoBox\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = rule.styleMap;
\f[B]const\f[R] width = styleMap.get(\(dqwidth\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] fontSize = styleMap.get(\(dqfont\-size\(dq);
.EE
.PP
We then log the type and value of the CSS Typed OM representations,
followed by the computed (resolved) values.
.IP
.EX
log(\(dqwidth\(dq);
log(\(ga type: ${width.constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(ga value: ${width}\(ga);
log(\(ga resolved: ${getComputedStyle(demoBox).width}\(ga);

log(\(dq\(rsnfont\-size\(dq);
log(\(ga type: ${fontSize.constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(ga values: [${[...fontSize.values].join(\(dq, \(dq)}]\(ga);
log(\(ga resolved: ${getComputedStyle(demoBox).fontSize}\(ga);
.EE
.SS Result
\f[CR]width\f[R] is represented by a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] object,
which has a value that matches the resolved width.
\f[CR]font\-size\f[R] is represented by a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] object
that exposes the \f[CR]calc()\f[R] sum\(cqs original terms.
